  "raw": " all-conquering Park.\n\nAmericans Jessica Korda and Austin Ernst won a tight women's final round at Mission Hills with a bogey ball, playing with 2016 British Open champion Karrie Webb in Arizona in July.\n\nThat helped them finish 10 shots ahead of Charley Hull and In Gee Chun.\n\nWorld number one Park ended up 12th in Arizona. She had been tightlipped about relations with caddie/mentor Pak Seonwoo prior to 2014 US Women's Open.\n\nHer winner's pay cheque was 1m ($US681,000) but she lost 3.34m back home for failing to be represented on her country flag as it was unfurled live because rules had been broken.\n\nThe awarded prize would have increased had Park won an Olympic gold medal or Spanish tour title - on both occasions her participation was ruled out by injury.\n\nTelevision coverage: 8pm BST on BBC Two Wales;",
  "serialized": "all-conquering Park. Americans Jessica Korda and Austin Ernst won a tight women's final round at Mission Hills with a bogey ball, playing with 2016 British Open champion Karrie Webb in Arizona in July. That helped them finish 10 shots ahead of Charley Hull and In Gee Chun. World number one Park ended up 12th in Arizona. She had been tightlipped about relations with caddie/mentor Pak Seonwoo prior to 2014 US Women's Open. Her winner's pay cheque was 1m ($US681,000) but she lost 3.34m back home for failing to be represented on her country flag as it was unfurled live because rules had been broken. The awarded prize would have increased had Park won an Olympic gold medal or Spanish tour title - on both occasions her participation was ruled out by injury. Television coverage: 8pm BST on BBC Two Wales;",
